# Test projects a change makes pass that the baseline's run of failed - a
# program the compiler built and ran wrong, or a refusal whose report lacked
# what the project expects.  One per line, the project's directory name under
# tests/tests/projects, then the reason.  A program the baseline REFUSES and
# the change makes compile goes in tests/started-compiling instead.
#
# `make verify ARGS="--baseline REV"` applies the lines this file carries and
# REV's copy does not.  It asserts that the baseline's test census fails on
# exactly the projects the two files declare, and the tree's census passing
# them is the rest of the claim.  Their objects are left out of the
# comparison: what the baseline compiled for them is the program being
# corrected.  A line stays once committed: against a later baseline it is
# inert, against an earlier one it is asserted again.
closure_struct_name_is_generated a closure's struct is a generated definition, so a program's own `__Closure_0` no longer becomes the closure's struct and call
link_failure_carries_linker_report a failed link's error carries the linker's own output, the reason, as a note
import_type_beside_function_meets_module an import binds every declaration a module offers under the leaf, so a type declared after a same-leaf function still meets a module of that name (E0205) instead of the function hiding it
static_call_undeclared_type a static call on a type the writer's scope does not name is E0203 at the qualifier, where it was a locationless E0900 count of unanswered path nodes
match_string_pattern_on_struct a literal pattern whose kind is not the subject's own type is E0200 at the pattern, where a string pattern on a struct compiled to an arm that never matched and the program returned 0
match_string_pattern_on_reference a string pattern on a reference to a string is E0200 at the pattern, where it compiled to an arm that never matched and the program returned 0
match_char_range_on_reference a char range on a reference to a char is E0200 at the pattern, where the check looked through the reference and the backend refused the pointer compare as an internal error (E0900)
spelling_lint_empty_reason an allow whose reason is empty or only spaces is E0152 at the reason, where it was E0152 for another cause: a lint level took identifiers only, and `reason = ...` was "argument 2 must be an identifier"
spelling_lint_missing_reason an allow of `lookup_by_spelling` with no reason is E0152, where lint levels were accepted and did nothing and the program built and returned 3
spelling_lint_refuses_unallowed a declaration taking a spelling type with no allow is E0157 at each such parameter - by value, by reference, as an array, a QualifiedName, and a method's non-receiver parameter - where the program built and returned 6
spelling_lint_directive_shapes a `deny` of the spelling lint leaves the parameter under it refused (E0157), where nothing refused it and only the four malformed directives were reported
array_method_argument_mismatch an argument of the wrong type to a dynamic array's method (push, insert, set, contains) is E0214 at the argument from the type check, where `cryo check` passed it and the build failed in codegen as "E0636: no method 'push' found on type 'i64[]'", then an unterminated block
bare_type_as_value_refused a bare identifier naming a type in an expression is refused where it is written - E0201 used as a value, E0231 called - where `Point(1, 2)` on a struct passed the type check and was refused only by code generation, and the others were reported as a value that does not exist
generic_receiver_other_instantiation_refused a method written for `Wrapper<B::Point>`, directly or through an alias of the owner, is E0358 on `Wrapper<A::Point>`, where the argument's last path segment matched and the program built and ran it on A's value
class_constructor_arguments_refused a construction's arguments are checked against the constructor of their arity, by `new C(args)` and by value `C(args)` (E0214 at a wrong type, E0215/E0216 at a count no constructor takes); the baseline built the program and ran it
compare_with_null_refused a struct, class or enum value, a number or a boolean compared with `null` or another pointer is refused by the type check (E0229); the baseline passed the check and then failed in code generation (E0633), or compiled a number compared with an address
generic_receiver_alias_refused a method whose receiver is written through a non-generic alias of `Wrapper<i64>` is E0358 on `Wrapper<i32>`, where a bare name in a receiver was taken to be the owner and the program built and ran it, reading the four-byte value as eight
overload_receiver_consumes_by_pin whether a method call consumes its receiver is asked of the overload it was pinned to, so a borrowing overload beside a consuming one of the same name no longer skips the receiver's drop - the program exited 2
trait_default_this_calls_typed a call on `this` in a trait's default method is typed by the trait's own declaration of the method, in a default with type parameters of its own and in one without, so `const s: string = this.count();` is E0200 there; the baseline left the call untyped and built the program
type_declaration_bound_types_calls a call on a value of a type parameter bounded by a `where` clause on the type's own declaration is typed by the bound's trait in the methods the declaration holds, so `const s: string = this.item.size();` is E0200 there; the baseline left the call untyped and built the program
